om the context, we know the squirrel is green and rough.\n   - Since the squirrel is rough, it is big (as per the given information that rough things are big).\nThe statement "If something is blue then it chases the lion" implies that blue things do not chase the lion.\nThe squirrel does not chase the lion, but this does not necessarily mean the squirrel is not blue.\nThe statement "If something chases the lion and it eats the squirrel then the squirrel sees the tiger" does not directly apply to the squirrel\'s color.\nThe statement "If the squirrel eats the lion and the squirrel is green then the lion sees the tiger" does not apply since the squirrel has not eaten the lion.\nThe statement "If something sees the tiger then it is blue" does not apply since the tiger is not blue.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**\n- The squirrel is green and rough, and we do not have any direct information that the squirrel is not blue.\n- The squirrel does not chase the lion, but this does not imply the squirrel is not blue.\n- The given conditions do not provide any information that directly states the squirrel is blue or not blue.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "The squirrel is not blue" is not confirmed.\n</think>\n<answer>\nConfirmed\n</answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
